	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Exposure is a process-focused photography mod. Load compatible film into the camera, use the viewfinder and learn its controls before spending a rare moment on an accidental frame."
				"Start in daylight with a still subject. Photograph the same build from several distances so you can see what framing changes without blaming every result on the film."
				"Keep spare film and a written shot list in the expedition backpack. The camera is most useful when the group knows what story it hopes to bring home."
				"Exposure albums tell stories in sequence. Name each volume, separate master photographs from travelling copies, and add written context when the image alone cannot explain location or danger."
			]
			id: "48734150D1E23719"
			rewards: [{
				id: "115877F719DB4D67"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A camera needs film and a deliberate subject"
			tasks: [{
				id: "73A70A13A112060A"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Exposure Camera Kit"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["48734150D1E23719"]
			description: [
				"Exposure models light-sensitive film and camera settings rather than producing a perfect screenshot every time. Brighter scenes tolerate easier settings; dark interiors require more care."
				"Use a tripod or stable position for planned portraits and structures. Fast creatures and aircraft need a different approach from a still museum object."
				"If an image fails, record the conditions and change one setting at a time. Photography becomes understandable when experiments are comparable."
				"Photography records both beauty and procedure. Capture portals, machine layouts, dungeon entrances, crop tests, and rare creatures as well as scenic views so the archive becomes a practical manual."
			]
			id: "0132E975CB7EC479"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4EA1A7481E8AEEC9"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Darkness, motion and distance are photographic choices"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5911E07854B62E52"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Read the Light"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["48734150D1E23719"]
			description: [
				"Exposed film must be developed using Exposure's Lightroom and the materials shown by JEI. Keep undeveloped and developed rolls in separate labelled storage."
				"Develop a test roll before a long journey so everyone understands the workflow. Make copies of irreplaceable pictures before placing them in risky builds."
				"A public darkroom needs input, output and archive areas. Do not let unique negatives vanish into the same chest as blank film."
				"Exposure albums tell stories in sequence. Name each volume, separate master photographs from travelling copies, and add written context when the image alone cannot explain location or danger."
			]
			id: "127F877D1BAD8DE2"
			rewards: [{
				id: "64471978F109D5DB"
