		{
			dependencies: ["127F877D1BAD8DE2", "5AA42D581850106D"]
			description: [
				"An album can show departure, route, discovery, danger and return. Arrange photographs so someone who was absent can understand what happened."
				"Add captions through nearby signs, books or named displays. Coordinates alone are useful; a sentence about why the place mattered is memorable."
				"Keep themed albums for dimensions, wildlife, factories and settlement history rather than one enormous pile of unrelated images."
				"Exposure albums tell stories in sequence. Name each volume, separate master photographs from travelling copies, and add written context when the image alone cannot explain location or danger."
				"The Archive Law says collection becomes culture only when others can understand it. Curate fewer objects with clearer stories, protect originals, and leave room for future players to add their own evidence."
			]
			id: "6A9FA5C21DC2E03D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1C624142C7E58019"
