			description: [
				"Create sections for settlements, machines, dimensions, creatures and unresolved mysteries. Give each section space for objects and written notes."
				"Keep irreplaceable originals protected and use copies or representative displays in public rooms. Store coordinates and access instructions beside the exhibit."
				"Invite each player to contribute one item and its story. A museum built by one collector is a collection; an archive built by the group is history."
				"The Archive Law says collection becomes culture only when others can understand it. Curate fewer objects with clearer stories, protect originals, and leave room for future players to add their own evidence."
